    <mediaPropertyAltText>
      <Value><![CDATA[The west front of Burghley House on a bright day, the grand Elizabethan stone facade and skyline of towers and chimneys reflected in calm water in the foreground.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyAltText>
    <mediaPropertyCountry>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "United Kingdom"
]]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyCountry>
    <mediaPropertyDescription>
      <Value><![CDATA[One of the grandest houses of the first Elizabethan age, built and largely designed by William Cecil, Lord High Treasurer to Queen Elizabeth I, between 1555 and 1587, with State Rooms decorated by Antonio Verrio and a deer park landscaped by Capability Brown.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyDescription>
